{"id": "r169-v4-code_task-05-en", "config": "grounded-v2", "reply": "```python\ndef interleave(xs, ys):\n    \"\"\"\n    Return a new list containing the items from xs and ys interleaved\n    such that the first element comes from xs, the second from ys,\n    the third from xs etc.  If one of the sequences is longer, the\n    remaining items are appended at the end.\n\n    Parameters\n    ----------\n    xs : iterable\n        The first sequence of items.\n    ys : iterable\n        The second sequence of items.\n\n    Returns\n    -------\n    list\n        A list with the interleaved elements.\n    \"\"\"\n    from itertools import zip_longest\n\n    # Use a unique sentinel to detect missing values\n    sentinel = object()\n    result = []\n\n    for a, b in zip_longest(xs, ys, fillvalue=sentinel):\n        if a is not sentinel:\n            result.append(a)\n        if b is not sentinel:\n            result.append(b)\n    return result\n```", "model": "keyless:gpt-oss-20b", "error": null, "code": "def interleave(xs, ys):\n    \"\"\"\n    Return a new list containing the items from xs and ys interleaved\n    such that the first element comes from xs, the second from ys,\n    the third from xs etc.  If one of the sequences is longer, the\n    remaining items are appended at the end.\n\n    Parameters\n    ----------\n    xs : iterable\n        The first sequence of items.\n    ys : iterable\n        The second sequence of items.\n\n    Returns\n    -------\n    list\n        A list with the interleaved elements.\n    \"\"\"\n    from itertools import zip_longest\n\n    # Use a unique sentinel to detect missing values\n    sentinel = object()\n    result = []\n\n    for a, b in zip_longest(xs, ys, fillvalue=sentinel):\n        if a is not sentinel:\n            result.append(a)\n        if b is not sentinel:\n            result.append(b)\n    return result\n", "latency_s": 30.0, "score": {"id": "r169-v4-code_task-05-en", "lang": "en", "task_type": "code_task", "spli