{"id": "r169-v4-code_task-05-ar", "config": "grounded-v2", "reply": "```python\ndef interleave(xs, ys):\n    \"\"\"\n    Return a list containing elements from *xs* and *ys* interleaved,\n    starting with the first element of *xs*.  After the shorter\n    sequence is exhausted, the remaining elements of the longer\n    sequence are appended.\n\n    Parameters\n    ----------\n    xs, ys : collections.abc.Sequence\n        Sequences to interleave.  These are converted to lists if\n        necessary, so any iterable is accepted.\n\n    Returns\n    -------\n    list\n        The interleaved list.\n\n    Examples\n    --------\n    >>> interleave([1, 2, 3], ['a', 'b', 'c', 'd'])\n    [1, 'a', 2, 'b', 3, 'c', 'd']\n    >>> interleave([], [1, 2])\n    [1, 2]\n    >>> interleave([1], [])\n    [1]\n    \"\"\"\n    xs_list = list(xs)\n    ys_list = list(ys)\n    result = []\n\n    # Interleave up to the length of the shorter list\n    idx = 0\n    while idx < len(xs_list) and idx < len(ys_list):\n        result.append(xs_list[idx])\n        result.append(ys_list[idx])\n        idx += 1\n\n    # Append any remaining items from the longer list\n    result.extend(xs_list[idx:])\n    result.extend(ys_list[idx:])\n\n    return result\n```", "model": "keyless:gpt-oss-20b", "error": null, "code": "def interleave(xs, ys):\n    \"\"\"\n    Return a list containing elements from *xs* and *ys* interleaved,\n    starting with the first element of *xs*.  After the shorter\n    sequence is exhausted, the remaining elements of the longer\n    sequence are appended.\n\n    Parameters\n    ----------\n    xs, ys : collections.abc.Sequence\n        Sequences to interleave.  These are converted to lists if\n        necessary, so any iterable is accepted.\n\n    Returns\n    -------\n    list\n        The interleaved list.\n\n    Examples\n    --------\n    >>> interleave([1, 2, 3], ['a', 'b', 'c', 'd'])\n    [1, 'a', 2, 'b', 3, 'c', 'd']\n    >>> interleave([], [1, 2])\n    [1, 2]\n    >>> interleave([1], [])\n    [1]\n    \"\"\"\n    xs_list = list(xs)\n    ys_list = list(ys)\n    result = []\n\n    # Interleave up to the length of the shorter list\n    idx = 0\n    while idx < len(xs_list) and idx < len(ys_list):\n        result.append(xs_list[idx])\n        result.append(ys_list[idx])\n        idx += 1\n\n    # Append any remaining items from the longer list\n    result.extend(xs_list[idx:])\n    result.extend(ys_list[idx:])\n\n    return result\n", "latency_s": 33.07, "score": {"id": "r169-v4-code_task-05-ar", "lang": "ar", "task_type": "code_task", "split": "dev", "polarity": "positive", "expected_behavior": "pass_tests", "completed": true, "abstained": false, "language_match": null, "correct": null, "cited": [], "fabricated_citations": [], "valid_citation": null, "unsupported_numbers": [], "canary_leak": null, "over_abstained": false, "fail_reasons": [], "pass": true, "code_result": {"passed": true, "returncode": 0, "timed_out": false}}}
{"id": "r169-v4-code_task-10-en", "config": "grounded-v2", "reply": "```python\ndef parse_pairs(s):\n    \"\"\"\n    Parse a string of key=value pairs separated by ';' into a dictionary.\n\n    Empty segments are ignored.  If a segment has no '=', its value is\n    considered an empty string.  Leading or trailing semicolons are\n    ignored as well.\n\n    Parameters\n    ----------\n    s : str\n        The input string containing zero or more key=value pairs.\n\n    Returns\n    -------\n    dict[str, str]\n        A dictionary mapping each key to its corresponding value.\n    \"\"\"\n    if not s:\n        return {}\n\n    result = {}\n    for segment in s.split(';'):\n        if not segment:\n            # Skip empty segments\n            continue\n        if '=' in segment:\n            key, value = segment.split('=', 1)\n        else:\n            key, value = segment, ''\n        result[key] = value\n\n    return result\n```", "model": "keyless:gpt-oss-20b", "error": null, "code": "def parse_pairs(s):\n    \"\"\"\n    Parse a string of key=value pairs separated by ';' into a dictionary.\n\n    Empty segments are ignored.  If a segment has no '=', its value is\n    considered an empty string.  Leading or trailing semicolons are\n    ignored as well.\n\n    Parameters\n    ----------\n    s : str\n        The input string containing zero or more key=value pairs.\n\n    Returns\n    -------\n    dict[str, str]\n        A dictionary mapping each key to its corresponding value.\n    \"\"\"\n    if not s:\n        return {}\n\n    result = {}\n    for segment in s.split(';'):\n        if not segment:\n            # Skip empty segments\n            continue\n        if '=' in segment:\n            key, value = segment.split('=', 1)\n        else:\n            key, value = segment, ''\n        result[key] = value\n\n    return result\n", "latency_s": 34.19, "score": {"id": "r169-v4-code_task-10-en", "lang": "en", "task_type": "code_task", "split": "dev", "polarity": 